 @Zaaf2003  This is not an issue,    the engine will cull all unnecessary triangles of a scene during cpu instructions,  meaning your framerate will jump higher when less triangles are sent to the gpu.. this is how it should work. 
This also means source 1 & 2 is very fickle when it comes to having a lot of separate entities as it puts a higher load on the cpu (more objects = more work even when it comes to a single mesh/bsp)... it's one of the things respawn struggled with apex and titanfall as all of their maps are built up of massive amounts of entities.

It's one of those things engines like unreal engine struggle with as everything is separate objects, they work around this by batching everything together... but that also means their framerates are fairly stable but not as a high as they could be.

